<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
        The widget needs its own manifest. A privacy manifest describes the
        binary it ships in, and an app extension is a separate binary: the
        app's manifest lives under TimeCapsule/, which is synchronized to the
        app target only, so AtticWidget.appex was shipping without one at all
        while its compiled sources call a required-reason API. That is
        refused at upload with ITMS-91053, not at review.

        The declaration is deliberately minimal. Every required-reason API
        family was checked against this target's entire compiled source set —
        AtticWidget/ plus AtticShared/ — and two are present: UserDefaults,
        and file timestamps (below). MediaAssetLoading.swift's timestamp use
        belongs to the app target; the widget has its own.

        1C8F.1 is the designed access: AtticDefaults reads the App Group
        suite the app shares with this extension. CA92.1 is included because
        the same type falls back to `UserDefaults.standard` when the App
        Group is not provisioned, which is a reachable path rather than a
        hypothetical one — the release checklist treats provisioning that
        group as an outstanding step.
    -->
    <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
            <array>
                <string>1C8F.1</string>
                <string>CA92.1</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
        <!--
            WidgetPhotoStore in MemoryWidget.swift reads
            contentModificationDateKey to delete batches of saved widget
            photos once no timeline can still be showing them. Added with the
            rotating widget; before it, this target had no timestamp use and
            this manifest said so, which would have been refused at upload.

            C617.1 for the same reason as the app's: file metadata inside the
            extension's own container (its Caches), never shown to anyone.
        -->
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
            <array>
                <string>C617.1</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
    </array>
    <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
    <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
